{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact revised register packet head 6756b53c80878ccf64e851b25dd60441c00fa156 on builder/failed-claim-register-packet-20261105, tree 67a83c67, for request c448c870 under promise f9db5e9e and review request b0d59473. This approval covers the 14 paths at this head. It resolves blocking review bf2e724f. It approves the procedure and its tooling, not any live result: the planner's later record must show every actual value, deployment and check.\n\nScope. Main a4e62771 is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. The head adds eight commits over main, the branch is pushed, and the commit-message check passes for all eight. Every changed path is under notes/ or docs/. No production source, test, seal, dependency or live Wrangler file changes. apps/room/wrangler.demo.jsonc hashes to 87bb65bb… at both main and this head, as packet.json pins. After gate commit 3bd61d15, only the note, the procedure and the revision gate manifest change. The procedure change adds the Site baseline record before cutover.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Each finding from bf2e724f is resolved. The host source at a4e62771 gives both adapters, both Site paths, the Site token owner and the workspace path authority for every listed root. The procedure now requires three checks on old rooms after the switch, before the scratch room. An ordinary member makes a child birth under Register 17. A real `dap clone` succeeds from an existing old-room member home. The old room's Site serves a known file, compared against a URL and digest recorded before cutover. Each check stops the rollout when it fails. docs/deploy.md now describes the same-Worker cutover with these checks, and states the Grow archive limit.\n- Every stage keeps the old root. The install, offer and rollback templates all list the Register 17 root sc_b5q435os… together with the planned root. The renderer requires exactly that list, and it requires hostRegisterScopes to return the same list that readInstalledRegisters returns. Rollback restores the original REGISTER_SCOPE, Artifacts register and Register 17 offer, and keeps both roots listed. It also requires a real clone from any new-root TEST room. In each stage, REGISTER_SCOPE equals ARTIFACTS_CONFIG.registerScope, so the agreement rule from a4e62771 keeps the adapters open.\n- The renderer changes only what the stage needs. It refuses a changed base file, a non-variable Wrangler change and any variable outside the stage's set. It binds `main` to the reviewed checkout, writes a new mode-0600 file, and plans, signs and deploys nothing. In the install stage, production demoCreationConfig closes the Register 17 offer while the host names the planned root. The offer stage requires the actual installed incarnation and platform:register@26.\n- The synthetic checks show these behaviors. The corrected probe exits 0. All three stages render and pass the production checks. Six altered configurations refuse at the expected checks: a missing old root, a missing current root, a malformed list, a mismatched host register, a mismatched Page reference and an unfilled incarnation. All three unfilled templates refuse. Host policy refuses a conflicting current or configured root and keeps the single-root result without a list. The first probe attempt, which expected the wrong refusal message, stays retained.\n- The token scene stays honest. The observer retains only the TEST room's credential in new private custody and checks its digest across the hour. It compares the same expired token, refuses an early run and never calls `dap clone` for the comparison. The procedure states what the scene cannot prove about a clone already in progress at expiry.\n- The doc changes match the landed cohort. Register 26 closes a claim as failed on its last attempt when nothing is selected, which frees its place. A late confirmation goes only to cleanup. Register 17 keeps its pending behavior.\n- The gate passed. gate.exit reads exit 0 at 3bd61d15, tree ddd9d711: Node